# kitty startup session. Linked to ~/.config/kitty/ by ./scripts/link-kitty and
# selected by `startup_session` in kitty.conf.
#
# This applies to the FIRST window of a kitty instance only: boss.py's
# _new_os_window builds its session without default_session, so cmd+n, new tabs
# and new windows still give a plain shell. `kitty <command>` also bypasses it.
#
# Go through a login fish rather than exec'ing zellij directly. kitty.app is
# started by LaunchServices, so its PATH is only
#   /Applications/kitty.app/Contents/MacOS:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin
# and the zellij *server* inherits it. Interactive panes are unaffected (zellij
# execs $SHELL by absolute path), but resurrected panes exec their `command=`
# straight from that PATH, so `claude`, `bun` and friends came back "command not
# found". A login fish rebuilds PATH before zellij ever starts.
launch fish -l -c "exec zellij attach --create main"
